cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Redoubt in research or coursework, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Redoubt: a cross-view kernel-module rootkit detector for Linux and macOS"
abstract: >-
  Redoubt detects kernel-module rootkits by collecting the same kernel-level
  fact through several independent paths and reporting when they disagree.
  It is written in dependency-free C, is read-only, and runs on Linux and macOS.
authors:
  - family-names: Gokani
    given-names: Tej
repository-code: "https://github.com/tejgokani/redoubt"
url: "https://github.com/tejgokani/redoubt"
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-09-21"
keywords:
  - rootkit detection
  - kernel security
  - loadable kernel modules
  - cross-view analysis
  - Linux
  - macOS
  - digital forensics
  - incident response
